% A recursive rule that negates a relation of a lower stratum.  reach/1 is
% the set of rooms reachable from the hall without entering a locked one;
% locked/1 is complete before reach/1's fixed point begins, so every round,
% and every semi-naive delta variant, tests the same complete relation.
%
% The cellar is locked, so the vault beyond it is unreachable even though an
% unlocked corridor leads on from the cellar.  The attic is reached around
% the loop through the study.
door(hall, kitchen).
door(hall, cellar).
door(cellar, vault).
door(kitchen, study).
door(study, attic).
door(attic, kitchen).

locked(cellar).

reach(hall).
reach(Y) :- reach(X), door(X, Y), not locked(Y).

reach(X)?
